    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "24e523b53a659ea1e290e68687dae05fb77dd8ad1620ad699d4a9bd80df1f7f2",
      "text": "After breakfast, set out to learn about one of Colombia’s best-known products: coffee.\n\nHacienda Coloma is in the Fusagasugá area, about two hours by road from Bogotá. Coffee grows here among the mountains at more than 1,600 metres above sea level.\n\nAt the hacienda, you’ll see how coffee goes from planting and harvesting to processing, roasting and brewing. After a coffee tasting, head to the cellar to sample eight-year-old rum.\n\nEnd the visit with a traditional local lunch, then return to your hotel in Bogotá.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-1ec1641096b2",
        "model": "GPT-6 Codex"
      }
